      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Eric,\n\n1. Regarding the precedence :\nas described here for AudioPolicyManager::selectOutput() - https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/android15-qpr1-release:frameworks/av/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp;l\u003d2183?q\u003dAudioPolicyManager.cpp\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject\n   * output with higher channel count has precedence over the power saving mode.\n\n   This works well for the mixer multi-channel output path (non-direct path). \n\nHowever, for the DIRECT output path, same priorities aren\u0027t applied by the Audio Policy Manager.\nDirect output request for multi-channel track is rejected as it\u0027s requested with power saving mode. \n\n2. Regarding power saving mode:\n   The app doesn\u0027t request for power saving mode while creating a multi-channel audio track.The track buffer size (10 x frame size) set during AudioTrack creation forces the power saving mode because of this code in the frameworks: \n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/android15-qpr1-release:frameworks/base/media/java/android/media/AudioTrack.java;l\u003d1820?q\u003dshouldEnablePowerSaving\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject",
