      "side": 1,
      "message": "The DEEP buffer flag rejection in openDirectOutput() was added to fix b/357522537 which is actually a similar problem wehre both DEEP BUFFER and DIRECT flags were set when opening the audio HAL stream.\n\nWe need to define a policy for precendence between direct output and deep buffer and have a consisten implementaiton between routes using a DAP mix and other routes handled by getOutputForDevices.\n\nI can suggest that a direct output has precedence over a deep buffer request if there is a match on channel mask, sampling rate or format and that in this case we clear the DEEP buffer flag when opening the direct output.\n\nMikhail,\n\nyou have more context on b/357522537, what do you think?",
